     "title": "We Are Made of Star-Stuff, Sailing a Cosmic Sea",
     "content": "In 1980, Carl Sagan stood on a windswept California cliff and told **500 million viewers** something audacious: that they were part of an unimaginable vastness, and that the universe was knowable.\n\n**Cosmos: A Personal Voyage** opened with the line, *\"The cosmos is all that is or ever was or ever will be.\"*\n\nThis seminar updates Sagan's voyage with **four decades of new discovery**:\n• **Hubble** mapped the deep field (1995)\n• **JWST** opened the infrared sky (2022)\n• **LIGO** heard gravitational waves (2015)\n• **Event Horizon Telescope** photographed a black hole (2019)\n\nIn this first lesson, you'll learn the *scale* of the cosmos — how big, how old, and how we measure it. Sagan taught that **knowing our cosmic address** is the beginning of wisdom.",
