     "explanation": "Redshift z = 14.32 means the wavelength has stretched by a factor of 1 + z = 15.32 since the light was emitted. Using the standard cosmological model, this corresponds to light emitted when the universe was only ~290 million years old. The galaxy's *comoving* distance now is ~33 billion light-years (not 14.32 billion), and 'z' is a wavelength shift, not a date or distance directly.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Redshift and cosmic time</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"170\" width=\"900\" height=\"180\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"220\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">JADES-GS-z14-0</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"265\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">z = 14.32 (detected by JWST, 2024)</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"305\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Current record-holder for most distant galaxy</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"338\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">confirmed by NIRSpec spectroscopy</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"400\" width=\"900\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"450\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">REDSHIFT MEANING</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"490\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Wavelength stretched by factor (1 + z) = 15.32</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"530\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Space itself expanded during light's journey</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"610\" width=\"900\" height=\"180\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"660\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">TIME OF EMISSION</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"705\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">~290 million years after Big Bang</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"745\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Universe was &lt; 2% of its current age</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"780\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Galaxy already showed structure and stars</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"840\" width=\"700\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"885\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">WHY THIS MATTERS</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"930\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Galaxies formed earlier than expected</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"970\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Challenges some early-universe models</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1010\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">JWST is rewriting cosmic chronology</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Understanding redshift and time"
     }
