     "type": "practice",
     "title": "Practice: Trace Your Atoms' History",
     "content": "**Goal**: connect your own body to specific cosmic events.\n\n**For each element below, write where it likely originated**:\n\n**1. Hydrogen (in your water, your body 10% by mass)**\nOrigin: **Big Bang Nucleosynthesis**, t = 3 minutes\nAge: 13.8 billion years\nThese protons have been in your atoms longer than the Sun has existed.\n\n**2. Carbon (the basis of your organic chemistry, ~18% of your mass)**\nOrigin: **AGB stars** (medium-mass stars dying as planetary nebulae) AND core-collapse supernovae\nAge: at least a few hundred million years older than the Sun (~4.6 Gyr)\nEvery breath of CO₂ contains carbon forged in long-dead stars.\n\n**3. Oxygen (your air, your water, ~65% of your mass)**\nOrigin: **massive star core-collapse supernovae**\nAge: pre-solar\nEach breath inhales atoms ejected by violent stellar deaths.\n\n**4. Calcium (your bones, your teeth)**\nOrigin: **core-collapse supernovae**\nWithout massive stars dying, you would have no skeleton.\n\n**5. Iron (your blood hemoglobin, your metabolism)**\nOrigin: **Type Ia supernovae** + core-collapse SNe\nThe red color of your blood is **a fossilized stellar explosion**.\n\n**6. Gold or platinum (jewelry, if you wear any)**\nOrigin: **neutron star mergers** (confirmed by GW170817 in 2017)\nYour wedding ring is a kilonova relic.\n\n**Reflection**: take a moment and **literally touch your skin**. Every atom under your fingertip has a multi-billion-year cosmic history. **You are star archaeology made aware**.",
