     "explanation": "EHT imaged the bright accretion disk and photon ring around M87*. The dark center is the BLACK HOLE'S SHADOW — light from material behind the black hole is bent (or absorbed) so that we see no direct light from the central region. The shadow is ~2.6× the size of the event horizon due to gravitational lensing. The singularity itself is hidden inside and never visible. This is real reconstructed data from 8+ telescopes worldwide, not artistic rendering.",
