     "title": "Practice: Watch Astrobiology in Real Time",
     "content": "**Goal**: connect with the most exciting science of your lifetime.\n\n1. **Follow the JWST exoplanet program** at stsci.edu. List the next 3 exoplanets being targeted for atmospheric study.\n\n2. **Track K2-18 b news** — type \"K2-18 b 2025\" into a news search. What has happened since the 2023 DMS report?\n\n3. **Sign up for SETI Institute newsletter**. Check the **Breakthrough Listen** project — are we picking up signals from anywhere?\n\n4. **Download exoplanet.eu app** — browse the catalog. Sort by \"habitable\" — pick the closest one. That's your favorite alien sun.\n\n5. **Re-watch Cosmos episode 12** (Encyclopaedia Galactica) — Sagan's musings on extraterrestrial intelligence. Note his Drake Equation discussion.\n\n6. **Pick your favorite Fermi explanation**. Justify it in a paragraph. Defend it to a friend. This is real science — and it's interpretation. Citizens get to vote.\n\n**Bonus**: visit **Arecibo Message** (1974) — the radio signal we beamed at M13. It will arrive in 25,000 years. Sagan helped write it.",
