     "explanation": "In a cluster collision, the galaxies are mostly empty space and pass through each other (and the gas) with negligible interaction. The hot intergalactic gas — which contains most of the cluster's normal mass — actually collides hydrodynamically and slows down. Dark matter, if it interacts only via gravity, also passes through without slowing — so it stays with the galaxies, NOT with the gas. The displacement we see (revealed by gravitational lensing) demands a non-interacting mass component beyond ordinary matter.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Dark matter's collisionless nature</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"170\" width=\"450\" height=\"220\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"305\" y=\"215\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">DARK MATTER</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"260\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Only feels gravity</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"295\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">No EM, no nuclear force</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"330\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Passes through itself</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"365\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Goes with the galaxies</text><rect x=\"570\" y=\"170\" width=\"450\" height=\"220\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"795\" y=\"215\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">HOT GAS</text><text x=\"795\" y=\"260\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Charged particles</text><text x=\"795\" y=\"295\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">EM interactions slow it</text><text x=\"795\" y=\"330\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Heats up, X-rays out</text><text x=\"795\" y=\"365\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Stays behind at impact</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"430\" width=\"900\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"475\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">SEPARATION OBSERVED</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"520\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Lensing mass ≠ gas mass</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"555\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Spatially distinct — proven 2006</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"620\" width=\"900\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"665\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">RULES OUT MOND</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"710\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Modified gravity would track gas</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"745\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">But lensing tracks galaxies instead</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"810\" width=\"700\" height=\"230\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"855\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">WHAT WE DON'T KNOW</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"900\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Particle identity of DM is unknown</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"935\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">WIMPs, axions, or something stranger?</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"975\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Dozens of detector experiments running</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1015\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">No confirmed direct detection — 2025</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Two materials with different physics, one collision"
     }
