     "explanation": "If Λ remains constant, accelerating expansion will continue forever. Eventually galaxies beyond the cosmic event horizon will appear to recede faster than light. Existing galaxies will exhaust their gas, stars will burn out (max 10¹⁴ years), and only black holes will remain. Over 10⁶⁷ to 10¹⁰⁰ years, even black holes evaporate via Hawking radiation. The universe ends in 'heat death' — a thin, near-empty, cold, structureless soup at maximum entropy. The Big Crunch was the old assumption when expansion was thought to be decelerating; Λ rules it out.",
