     "type": "practice",
     "title": "Practice Problem: Estimate the Chemistry Timeline",
     "content": "**Goal**: get a feel for how fast (or slow) life could appear.\n\n**Given**:\n• Earth formed: **4.54 Gyr ago**\n• Surface habitable (post-bombardment): **4.0 Gyr ago**\n• Earliest microfossils (Pilbara, Australia): **3.5 Gyr ago**\n• First clear biological isotope signature: **3.7-3.8 Gyr ago**\n• Last Universal Common Ancestor (LUCA): **3.5-4.0 Gyr ago** (deeply uncertain)\n\n**Window for abiogenesis**: ~200-500 million years from \"habitable\" to \"life present.\"\n\n**Problem 1**: What does this fast timescale suggest about the difficulty of abiogenesis?\n\n*Answer*: Either (a) it's easier than once thought, (b) Earth had favorable conditions, or (c) life was seeded from elsewhere. It does NOT suggest \"impossibly rare\" — that would predict longer waiting times.\n\n**Problem 2**: Compare to the **lifetime of the Sun (10 Gyr)**. What fraction of stellar life was needed for biology to appear?\n\nLife appeared in **~10%** of the Sun's lifetime. If most stars allow this rapidly, the cosmos has plenty of time for life elsewhere.\n\n**Problem 3**: Now consider **M-dwarfs** with lifetimes of 100 Gyr. They've had **20× more time** than the Sun. Yet TRAPPIST-1 and similar systems may have lost atmospheres. **Time alone doesn't guarantee life — conditions must persist**.\n\n**Reflection**: the speed of Earth's abiogenesis is the **single most important clue** that life may not be uncommon. It's why Sagan was an optimist. But we have a sample of one — we cannot generalize confidently.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">PRACTICE PROBLEM</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Was Earth's abiogenesis fast?</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"170\" width=\"900\" height=\"120\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"215\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">EARTH FORMED</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"250\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">4.54 Gyr ago</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"278\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">From the protoplanetary disk</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"305\" width=\"900\" height=\"120\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"350\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">HABITABLE</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"385\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">4.0 Gyr ago</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"413\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">After Late Heavy Bombardment</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"440\" width=\"900\" height=\"120\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"485\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">FIRST LIFE SIGNS</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"520\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">3.7-3.8 Gyr ago (isotope signatures)</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"548\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">3.5 Gyr ago (microfossils)</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"575\" width=\"900\" height=\"120\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"620\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">WINDOW</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"655\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">200-500 Myr from habitable to life</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"683\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Fast — only ~10% of Sun's lifetime</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"710\" width=\"900\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.12)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"755\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">IMPLICATION</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Abiogenesis may not be rare</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"835\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Time alone doesn't guarantee — conditions matter</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"900\" width=\"700\" height=\"140\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"945\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">SAGAN'S OPTIMISM</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"985\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Built on this fast timescale</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1020\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Sample of 1: still cannot generalize</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Earth's fast timeline is hopeful for cosmic life"
     }
