     "explanation": "Sagan's BDK is fundamentally about avoiding intellectual self-deception. Its central themes include independent confirmation, encouraging substantive debate, spinning multiple hypotheses, judging your own ideas as harshly as others', quantifying when possible, and requiring testable (falsifiable) claims. Authority worship and majoritarianism are exactly what the kit guards against — Sagan repeatedly notes that 'authorities' have been wrong many times, and that popularity of a view is unrelated to its truth.",
